Alternative method through the system registry for Windows 10:

HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\Dnscache\Parameters

---------------------------------------------------------------

You need to register Quad9 or Cloudflare directly in the system's DoH database.

HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\Dnscache\Parameters\

DohWellKnownServers(If the subfolder DohWellKnownServers does not exist, right-click the Parameters folder, select New -> Key and name it DohWellKnownServers). 
Right-click the DohWellKnownServers folder, select New -> Key and create a subfolder named after the chosen server 
(e.g., Quad9 or Cloudflare). Enter the newly created subfolder and create two string values (right-click -> New -> String Value)

For Quad9: create a string value named Template and set its value to:

https://dns.quad9.net/dns-query


Also add a string value named ServerAddress and set its value to: 9.9.9.9


***********************************************************************************

For Cloudflare: create a string value named Template and set its value to: 

https://cloudflare-dns.com/dns-query

Also add a string value named ServerAddress and set its value to: 1.1.1.1

(If the DNSClient folder does not exist inside Windows NT, right-click Windows NT, add New -> Key and create it). 
Inside the DNSClient folder, right-click in the right pane, select New -> DWORD (32-bit) Value. Name it DoHPolicy  
and enter the value 3 (meaning no consent for unencrypted queries).

HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\Software\Policies\Microsoft\Windows NT\DNSClient

***********************************************************************************

To set the DNS server address on the network adapter, go to the network adapter settings  
(Control Panel -> Network and Internet -> Network and Sharing Center) and set the DNS server address entered earlier in the registry 
(9.9.9.9 for Quad9 or 1.1.1.1 for Cloudflare) as the Preferred DNS server.

How to check whether DoH is in use: 
ipconfig

